{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'P=/tmp/current-fresh3/current/workspace/basic-test-proof-current-20260811t112337z-current-fresh3-isolated-plan\nS=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T112337Z-current-fresh3/current/worker/planning/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \"No button-chain.html file exists in this planning proof, and none should be created until a future execution session starts. The task contract and work-unit inventory define the expected file, DOM, behavior, and styling.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \"This goal creates the complete future user-facing behavior and owns the primary browser story that proves it. Without these work units, there is no page, append logic, completion branch, visible white-bordered finished state, or direct-click evidence.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"W01 enables W02 by providing the root container. W02 enables W03 by defining append behavior. W03 enables W04 by centralizing click routing. W04 enables W05 by defining the completion DOM state. W06 depends on W01 through W05 and hands browser evidence to the static audit goal.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Use an explicit generated index for appended buttons so the initial button is not counted as generated. Ensure handleButtonClick() compares the clicked button with the current last button before acting. The fourth generated button must finish rather than append; earlier generated buttons append exactly one successor.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \"This goal starts only after goal 01 hands off an implemented button-chain.html and a passed or actionable US-01 browser result. In this planning proof, the static audit is specified but not executed.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \"The static audit catches acceptance-critical omissions that can be missed when a browser path passes accidentally, such as extra HTML artifacts, incorrect literal text, or missing self-contained handlers/styles.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"W07 depends on W01 through W05 and should be run after W06. Its handoff is a concise evidence note that button-chain.html is the only implementation artifact and contains the expected contract pieces.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Inspect only the implemented button-chain.html and the isolated workspace artifact list. Do not create new files during verification. If the audit finds a mismatch, record it in the bug register and add investigation/fix work before claiming completion.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/01-step-initial-markup instructions -p 5.1: \"During future execution, create button-chain.html as a standalone HTML document whose body contains one named root subtree #button-chain-root and exactly one visible initial button. Do not include generated buttons in the initial DOM.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/01-step-initial-markup acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"A fresh browser load of the future file shows exactly one button before interaction, and the DOM root for the chain is #button-chain-root.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/01-step-initial-markup handoff -p 7.1: \"W02 can rely on #button-chain-root existing and containing the initial button as the first current last button.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/02-step-append-function instructions -p 5.1: \"During future execution, add appendGeneratedButton() in button-chain.html. It creates one generated button with a generated index one greater than the current generated count and inserts it directly below the current last button.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/02-step-append-function acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Each call to appendGeneratedButton() increases the visible generated-button count by exactly one and preserves vertical order below the previous last button.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/02-step-append-function handoff -p 7.1: \"W03 can call appendGeneratedButton() after confirming the clicked button is eligible to act.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/03-step-last-button-handler instructions -p 5.1: \"During future execution, implement handleButtonClick() so it first determines the current last visible button in the chain. If the clicked button is not that last button, return without appending or finishing.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/03-step-last-button-handler acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Only a click on the current last button can change the document; earlier buttons remain inert after later buttons exist.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/03-step-last-button-handler handoff -p 7.1: \"W04 can add completion branching inside the same click handler without weakening the last-button guard.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/04-step-fourth-generated-finish instructions -p 5.1: \"During future execution, extend handleButtonClick() so a click on generated button 4 clears the document body and renders the completion state instead of calling appendGeneratedButton(). Generated buttons 1 through 3 continue to append exactly one next button.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/04-step-fourth-generated-finish acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"After the sequence initial, generated 1, generated 2, generated 3, generated 4 is clicked, no chain buttons remain and no generated button 5 is appended.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/04-step-fourth-generated-finish handoff -p 7.1: \"W05 can style the rendered completion element created by this branch.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/05-step-completion-style instructions -p 5.1: \"During future execution, style .completion-state so it contains exact text finished and has a visible white border against the page background. Keep the text lowercase and do not add surrounding words.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/05-step-completion-style acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"The final visible completion element reads exactly finished and its border is visibly white.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/05-step-completion-style handoff -p 7.1: \"W06 can use the visible completion element as the decisive browser assertion.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/06-step-browser-story instructions -p 5.1: \"After future implementation, run US-01 through the browser using direct mouse clicks only. Click the initial button, then generated buttons 1, 2, 3, and 4 as each becomes the current last visible button. Do not use console, injected JavaScript, storage edits, or direct API calls.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/06-step-browser-story acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"US-01 passes only when the first four clicks each append exactly one lower button and the fifth click clears the document to exact text finished with a visible white border. Record route, click sequence, and observed result in ui-story-runs/US-01.md.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/06-step-browser-story handoff -p 7.1: \"W07 can rely on the browser evidence or, if it fails, on the bug register entry and new investigation/fix scope.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain/02-step-static-audit instructions -p 5.1: \"After future implementation and US-01, inspect button-chain.html and the isolated workspace artifact list. Confirm the file is self-contained and no other HTML or HTM artifacts are part of the implementation.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain/02-step-static-audit acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"The audit records button-chain.html as the only future implementation HTML file and confirms the exact finished literal, .completion-state selector, appendGeneratedButton(), handleButtonClick(), and fourth-generated completion contract are present.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain/02-step-static-audit handoff -p 7.1: \"The initiative can be marked ready only when W06 and W07 both have passing evidence and the bug register has no open issue.\"\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
