{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'P=/tmp/current-fresh3/current/workspace/basic-test-proof-current-20260811t112337z-current-fresh3-isolated-plan\nS=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T112337Z-current-fresh3/current/worker/planning/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\n\"$S\" --description-section \"$P\" approach -p 4.1: \"Build the future file in atomic slices: initial DOM, append helper, last-button event routing, fourth-generated completion text branch, and completion border styling. Then run two planned UI stories with real clicks and a static audit to prove the acceptance contract.\"\n\"$S\" --description-section \"$P\" risks-and-open-questions -p 8.1: \"Main execution risks are off-by-one counting of generated buttons, allowing earlier non-last buttons to append, appending a fifth generated button instead of finishing, placing the exact finished text in the wrong work unit, or styling a border that is not visibly white. No user clarification is required because the task contract fixes the filename, behavior, text, and border visibility.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"W01 enables W02 by providing the root container. W02 enables W03 by defining append behavior. W03 enables W04 by centralizing click routing. W04 renders the exact finished text and enables W05 border styling. W06 depends on W01 through W05 for the completion story, and W08 depends on W01 through W03 for the non-last inert story.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Use an explicit generated index for appended buttons so the initial button is not counted as generated. Ensure handleButtonClick() compares the clicked button with the current last button before acting. The fourth generated button must clear the body and render exact text finished rather than append; earlier generated buttons append exactly one successor, and earlier non-last buttons remain inert.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \"This goal starts only after goal 01 hands off an implemented button-chain.html with completed browser story evidence for US-01 and US-02, or a recorded bug path if either story fails. In this planning proof, the static audit is specified but not executed.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"W07 depends on W01 through W06 and should be run after the completion browser story. It also considers W08 evidence when checking the last-button guard contract. Its handoff is a concise evidence note that button-chain.html is the only implementation artifact and contains the expected contract pieces.\"\n\"$S\" --goal-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain goal-size-exception -p 11.1: \"This is a standalone verification goal with one work unit, W07. The planning contract allows a single-work-unit goal for an independently demonstrable verification outcome.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/04-step-fourth-generated-finish instructions -p 5.1: \"During future execution, extend handleButtonClick() so a click on generated button 4 clears the document body and renders a completion element whose text content is exactly finished. This branch must not call appendGeneratedButton(); generated buttons 1 through 3 continue to append exactly one next button.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/04-step-fourth-generated-finish acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"After the sequence initial, generated 1, generated 2, generated 3, generated 4 is clicked, no chain buttons remain, no generated button 5 is appended, and the completion element text is exactly finished.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/04-step-fourth-generated-finish handoff -p 7.1: \"W05 can style the completion element and must preserve the exact finished text rendered by this branch.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/05-step-completion-style instructions -p 5.1: \"During future execution, style .completion-state with a visible white border against the page background. Do not create or change the semantic completion text in this style work unit.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/05-step-completion-style acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"The final visible completion element keeps the exact text finished from W04 and has a visibly white border supplied by .completion-state.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/05-step-completion-style handoff -p 7.1: \"W06 can use the exact text from W04 and white border from W05 as separate browser assertions.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/07-step-non-last-inert-story instructions -p 5.1: \"After future implementation, run US-02 through the browser using direct mouse clicks only. Create at least two generated buttons through valid current-last clicks, then click an earlier button that is no longer last. Do not use console, injected JavaScript, storage edits, or direct API calls.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/07-step-non-last-inert-story acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"US-02 passes only when the non-last click leaves the button count unchanged, does not clear the document, and does not show finished. Record route, click sequence, before/after count, and observed result in ui-story-runs/US-02.md.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 01-build-button-chain/07-step-non-last-inert-story handoff -p 7.1: \"W07 can cite US-02 evidence for the last-button guard contract during the static audit.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain/02-step-static-audit instructions -p 5.1: \"After future implementation and after W06 browser verification, inspect button-chain.html and the isolated workspace artifact list. Confirm the file is self-contained and no other HTML or HTM artifacts are part of the implementation. Include W08 evidence when checking the non-last guard contract.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain/02-step-static-audit acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"The audit records button-chain.html as the only future implementation HTML file and confirms the exact finished literal is rendered by the completion branch, .completion-state supplies a white border, appendGeneratedButton(), handleButtonClick(), last-button guard, and fourth-generated completion contract are present.\"\n\"$S\" --step-section \"$P\" 02-verify-button-chain/02-step-static-audit handoff -p 7.1: \"The initiative can be marked ready only when W06, W08, and W07 all have passing evidence and the bug register has no open issue.\"\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
